          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "From these two regulated rails, 3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The +3V3 domain has no regulator connection in the netlist, so its pull-ups and connector supply pins would be unpowered on the board; the separate equal-voltage SPICE sources mask this disconnection in simulation.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["FCC2", "UART3_FCC2"],
      "pins": ["FCC2.48", "FCC2.73", "UART3_FCC2.3", "UART3_FCC2.4"],
      "nets": ["NET0109", "NET0110"],
      "observed": "FCC2's two VCAP pins are connected directly to pins 3 and 4 of the UART3_FCC2 connector.",
      "expected": "VCAP pins are MCU internal-regulator capacitor connections and should not serve as UART signals or be exposed as such; UART connector pins should connect to the intended UART TX/RX signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(name \"NET0109\") ... (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\") ... (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"3\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(name \"NET0110\") ... (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\") ... (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"4\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART3 connector does not provide proper UART signals on these pins, and external loading through the connector can disrupt the MCU's internal regulator supply.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: both MCUs have unconnected VDD pins, the regulated +3.3V output is isolated from a separate +3V3 distribution net, and FCC VCAP pins are routed to a UART connector. These connectivity faults would prevent normal board operation and compromise the UART interface."
}

